# SYNOPSIS

```usage
lua /lib/wm/wm.lua
```

# DESCRIPTION

`wm` is the desktop's policy (03 §5.2-5.3), a Lua program with the whole `/wsys` tree, its grant (boot/svc/wm.ndb).
It gives winsrv(8) the key bindings in `/lib/wm/keys.ndb`, which winsrv matches in its own input path, so they work while `wm` is busy.
It follows `/wsys/events` and places windows: where winsrv puts them while the layout is `float`, and master-stack while it is `tile` (dwm's: the oldest window on the left half, the rest down the right half, 8 pixels apart).

A binding's verb winsrv cannot do itself comes to `wm`: `layout tile` and `layout float` change the layout; `spawn NAME` starts a program, once there is one to start (the terminal is M7 step 7f).

It starts with `vx.desktop` on the kernel command line, and is restarted if it exits.

# FILES

: `/lib/wm/keys.ndb`
  The bindings it gives winsrv: super+t tiles, super+f floats, super+j and super+k move the focus, super+q closes the focused window, super+enter spawns a terminal.

